+`docs/handoff-glm.md` applies unchanged.** This brief is analysis first, then the packets it
+justifies; nothing under `strategy-lab/` is read or written.
+
+#### A1. Plan gap analysis
+`docs/PLAN.md` is the source of truth for the package (`src/yt_research/`, `mcp_server.py`,
+`cli.py`). Read it and `docs/ORIGINAL_PLAN.md`, then produce `docs/PLAN_STATUS_2026-09-13.md`:
+one row per planned item — implemented (with the module and a test that proves it), partial
+(what is missing), or absent. Evidence only from code and tests in this repository; where the
+plan is ambiguous, say so rather than decide.
+- Size: medium (reading).
+
+#### A2. Packets for the gaps
+For every *absent* or *partial* row that is pure library/CLI work with an offline test, append a
+packet in this file's format (location, acceptance test, size) under a new `## B` section, in
+the order the plan implies. Do not implement them under this brief; the coordinator orders them.
+- Size: small.
+
+#### A3. Integration readiness of `glm/board-audit`
+The branch is 30+ commits over `main`, all verified. Produce `docs/BOARD_AUDIT_INTEGRATION.md`:
+`git diff --stat main..glm/board-audit`, confirmation the merge is a fast-forward
+(`git merge-base --is-ancestor main glm/board-audit`), the test count on both, and the one
+command the operator runs. No merge.
+- Size: trivial.
+
+## B — packets for the gaps (generated by A1/A2, 2026-09-13)
+
+The plan-gap analysis (`docs/PLAN_STATUS_2026-09-13.md`) found exactly one
+partial row that is pure library work with an offline test: `get_metadata`'s
+extended-field mapping (`is_live`, `was_live`, `availability`, `tags`,
+`categories`, `chapters`) has no unit test asserting it against the
+committed `info_dict.json` fixture — it is only covered live (integration)
+or by CLI mocks. Everything else in both plan documents is implemented,
+implemented-and-superseded, or outside this review's reach, so there is
+exactly one packet. The coordinator orders it.
+
+#### B1. Unit-test the extended metadata mapping
+`src/yt_research/metadata.py::get_metadata` maps the committed
+`tests/fixtures/info_dict.json` to the public dict; assert every planned
+field — the original five (title, channel, duration, upload date, view
+count) plus `is_live`, `was_live`, `availability`, `tags`, `categories`,
+`chapters` (`metadata.py::_chapters`) — against that fixture offline, plus
+the degraded shapes (missing `chapters` → empty list, null `availability`
+passes through as null).
+- Tests: new `tests/test_metadata.py` (or a section in `tests/test_pipeline.py`),
+  fixture-only, no network.
+- Size: small.
+
+## Definition of done
+As brief 3. Report which plan rows you could not classify.
